  "verbalization": "Prednisone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Non-histaminic Angioedema through a chain of indications involving Triamcinolone. This relationship is supported by the shared indication of Triamcinolone with Non-histaminic Angioedema across three distinct pathways, each linking Prednisone to Triamcinolone via different clinical conditions. The presence of Triamcinolone as an indication for Non-histaminic Angioedema suggests a potential mechanistic link, though the exact nature of this relationship remains unclear. The pathways highlight that Prednisone may influence the development of Non-histaminic Angioedema through the activation of Triamcinolone, which in turn may contribute to the condition. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Triamcinolone in the pathophysiology of Non-histaminic Angioedema, though further research is needed to elucidate the precise mechanisms involved.",
